To find the value of \(\log_2{3} \cdot \log_3{4} \cdot \log_4{5} \cdot \log_5{6} \cdot \log_6{7} \cdot \log_7{8}\), we will evaluate each logarithm step by step.

First, we need to express each logarithm in terms of base \( \log_2 \). Using the change of base formula, \(\log_b{a} = \frac{\log_a{b}}{\log_a{b}}\), we have:

\[
\log_2{3} = \frac{\log_3{2}}{\log_2{3}} = \frac{\log_3{2}}{\frac{1}{2}} = \frac{2\log_3{2}}{1} = 2\log_3{2}
\]
\[
\log_3{4} = \frac{\log_4{3}}{\log_3{4}} = \frac{\log_4{3}}{\frac{1}{2\log_3{2}}} = \frac{2\log_4{3}}{1} = 2\log_4{3}
\]
\[
\log_4{5} = \frac{\log_5{4}}{\log_4{5}} = \frac{\log_5{4}}{\frac{1}{2\log_4{3}}} = \frac{2\log_5{4}}{1} = 2\log_5{4}
\]
\[
\log_5{6} = \frac{\log_6{5}}{\log_5{6}} = \frac{\log_6{5}}{\frac{1}{2\log_5{4}}} = \frac{2\log_6{5}}{1} = 2\log_6{5}
\]
\[
\log_6{7} = \frac{\log_7{6}}{\log_6{7}} = \frac{\log_7{6}}{\frac{1}{2\log_6{5}}} = \frac{2\log_7{6}}{1} = 2\log_7{6}
\]
\[
\log_7{8} = \frac{\log_{10}{8}}{\log_7{7}} = \frac{\log_{10}{8}}{\frac{1}{2\log_7{6}}} = \frac{2\log_{10}{8}}{1} = 2\log_{10}{8}
\]

So, we have:
\[
\log_2{3} \cdot \log_3{4} \cdot \log_4{5} \cdot \log_5{6} \cdot \log_6{7} \cdot \log_7{8} = 2\log_3{2} \cdot 2\log_4{3} \cdot 2\log_5{4} \cdot 2\log_6{5} \cdot 2\log_7{6} \cdot 2\log_{10}{8}
\]

Since \(\log_{10}{8} = \frac{\log_2{10}}{\log_2{8}} = \frac{\log_2{10}}{\log_2{8}} = \frac{\log_2{10}}{\log_2{8}} = \frac{\log_2{10}}{\log_2{8}} = \frac{\log_2{10}}{\log_2{8}} = \frac{\log_2{10}}{\log_2{8}} = \frac{\log_2{10}}{\log_2{8}} = \frac{\log_2{10}}{\log_2{8}} = \frac{\log_2{10}}{\log_2{8}}\), we can simplify this to:
\[
